# Local env files
# .env holds public config only (EXPO_PUBLIC_* is inlined into the bundle), but
# it stays untracked so a stray secret can never be committed by accident.
# Copy .env.example to .env to get started; CI/EAS supply these as build env vars.
#
# EVERY .env* spelling except the committed example. The pattern used to be
# `.env` plus `.env*.local`, which left `.env.development` and `.env.production`
# — filenames Expo's own tooling loads, and which this repo's guard suite
# already scans for key material — tracked if anyone created one.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# TypeScript
*.tsbuildinfo

# Generated native folders
/ios
/android
